: \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8c05331ef9d11d54fc96d87ad7ab91becdcc37c51395380bf65ae1ab558fb1bc","event_uuid":"4a76ed94-6538-497b-b15a-5e4f4bf5ad3e","position":{"commit_sha":"30e1a0d89f9823740ff5fa6e6df34f52a4c67712","position":"1792363167655989658-4a76ed94-6538-497b-b15a-5e4f4bf5ad3e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"274a293d6b08dd55768a542eaf2856e37bad403214387d33871bbf379f8a4610","event_uuid":"c64255c7-3859-41a8-8d1e-f2d4528c7554","position":{"commit_sha":"096e2af80a1fc7c79ddccc7b63bd02c5f00da35d","position":"1792363374040837964-c64255c7-3859-41a8-8d1e-f2d4528c7554"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"23237715f4e6aaaeb6c5d6027c5ab5bb0666e44b5563e5053291c587d31470b5","event_uuid":"e79f44a0-547b-4421-823c-5d6d3f79644f","position":{"commit_sha":"a1de5468f644867cfba81a0c039d3ddc1dbb18b4","position":"1792383357790647863-e79f44a0-547b-4421-823c-5d6d3f79644f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Audit findings that shape the stories (resolved, not reopened)\n\n- **Loader sites in `src`** (`git grep -lE 'lazy_load\\(|spec_from_file_location' origin/main -- src`): 47 files — 44 under `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` (every `try: from rebar_reconciler._loader import lazy_load / except ImportError:` prologue plus hand-rolled loaders in `__main__.py:116-170`, `applier.py:226-235`, `differ.py:44,84`, `fetcher.py:153`, `inbound_collection_diffs.py:60`, `inbound_fields.py:45`, `inbound_translate.py:121`, `invariants.py:68,90`, `last_pass.py:53-64`, `pass_io.py:51,69`, `binding_repository.py:298`, `outbound_pass.py:69`) and 3 outside: `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py:147-161` (`_ref_lock_module`), `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:161-173` (`_engine_module`), `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:367-378` (`_load_engine_mode` → `rebar._engine_mode`); plus `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py:31-35` and `bridge_fsck_visibility.py:36-50`. In-process `sys.path.insert(engine_dir)` sites: `_cli/__init__.py:148-151`, `_commands/_repair_pause.py:39-42`, `_commands/doctor_mapping.py:43-45`, `_commands/fsck_repair.py:344-347`. `src/rebar/graph/_loader.py:3` only mentions the idiom historically (no change).\n- **`sys.modules` keys** the source registers and tests pre-seed: dotted `rebar_reconciler.{_advisory_lock,mode,request,pass_support,_preflight,alert_store,mutation,config,link_direction,adapters.jira.adf,operation_outcome,failure_policy,git_adapter,observation,create_route,coordinator,ticket_planner,ticket_plan,runtime,retry_budget,reconcile_helpers,rebar_id_audit,persist_phase,pass_io,pass_fuse,manifest_renderer,load_phase,dispatch_one,create_coordinator,create_containment,apply_phase,apply_handlers,applier,_errors,batch_dispatch,binding_store,_ref_lock,_loader,__main__}`; flat keys `reconcile_helpers`, `pass_support`, `reconcile_mutation`, `rebar_reconciler_errors`, `rebar_reconciler__ref_lock_advisory`, `rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_advisory`, `rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_push`, `rebar_reconciler_config`, `rebar_reconciler_alert_store`, `reconcile_selection_binding_store`, `reconcile_run_differs`, `reconcile_config`, `reconcile_classify`, `reconcile_binding_walk`, `_concurrency`, `conflict_resolver`, `config`, `overview`, `rebar._engine_mode`, `rebar_reconciler_classify_fsck`; test-private keys (`applier`, `fetcher`, `reconcile_*`, `rebar_reconciler_advisory_lock`, `rebar_reconciler_mode`, ~60 per-file names). 343 test files / 442 `spec_from_file_location` sites; 149 files `import rebar_reconciler`.\n- **Test-side loader complex**: `tests/_engine_path.py` (canonical-root helper), `tests/conftest.py:462-505` (`_one_engine_root` autouse), `tests/unit/conftest.py:22-97` (shadow-package bridge), `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py:39-95`, `tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_load_module_identity.py`, `tests/_log_integrity.py:54` (`SHARED_LOGGER_NAMES` includes `rebar_reconciler`). `pyproject.toml:691-698` has `testpaths=[\"tests\"]` and no `pythonpath`/`rootdir` — the package rename needs no pytest config change.\n- **Ratchets keyed on paths (must be handled or CI is red)**: `.github/complexity-baseline.json` has 6 `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/...` keys (`outbound_fields.py::_diff_fields:32`, `applier.py::apply:22`, `binding_walk.py::compute_binding_walk_mutations:27`, `dispatch_one.py::create_one:36`, `inbound_differ.py::_diff_jira_vs_local:16`, `outbound_field_diff.py::diff_canonical_fields:23`); `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` has 29 `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` keys. A path move makes every one `new` → `make lint` fails. **Decision:** the move stories carry a value-preserving key re-spell (prefix rewrite only, counts/ceilings unchanged) — this is the maintenance path and requires **operator sanction** in the change (AGENTS.md forbids contributor hand-edits; flag on the Gerrit change).\n- **Already discharged on `origin/main`** (nothing to delete): `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` (absent, `mode.py:39-42`); `_ref_lock.py:717` writer now persists `\"dry-run\"` (`_PAUSE_GATED_MODE`, `:591`), decoder keeps `_PAUSE_LEGACY_GATED_MODES={\"reconcile-check\"}` (`:592`) — bug `extralegal-durative-beaver` is **closed** (Gerrit 2728). `mode.py:57` `from_str(\"reconcile-check\")→DRY_RUN` and `_ref_lock.py:592` are **kept** as persisted-pause-blob read compat. `MODE_CAPS` is live (`__main__.py:187`, `apply_planning.py:93`, `load_phase.py:165`, `ticket_planner.py:60`) and the bootstrap modes are live consumers (`reconcile-bridge.yml:59-60`, DC harness `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py:70`, `manifest_renderer.py`) — **kept**; only the MCP by-path load and the dead `ctx.MODE_CAPS`/`ctx.Mode` handles (`mcp_server.py:599-600`, no registrar reads them) are deleted.\n- **`disturbed-antiutopic-pullet`** is a `session_log` for epic RP-04 (`vibrant-legal-hind`, **closed**); its S3 landed `REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE` as the AC6 rollback switch and S7 (`junior-lepidolite-boa`, closed) checked \"legacy facades/switches removed\". It needs nothing; deleting the switch completes S7.\n- **`REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP`** readers: `apply_handlers.py:282,551,589`. It is set to `\"1\"` in the sole live deployment (`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml:287`). **Decision:** promote fail-loud to unconditional and delete the env var (no test hook, no injected parameter needed).\n- **`.rebar/` conventions**: `.gitignore:24` `.rebar/*` ignores everything under `.rebar/` with surgical un-ignores (`:25-47`: `metrics-snapshots.ndjson`, `backfill-close-class.ndjson`, `trusted_environments.yaml`, `criteria_routing.json`, `plan_review_moves.json`, `prompts/*`, `evals/*`). Runtime files already there: `current_session_log`, `hlc.lock/.state`, `gate_runs/`, `workflow_runs/`, `run_snapshots/`, `scratch/`, `cache/`, `usage.jsonl`, `enrich-drain.lock`, `compact-worker.lock`. `.rebar/bridge/` is covered by `.rebar/*`; **no new pattern needed**; `.gitignore:14` `bridge_state/` is deleted. `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` uses the git file list (bug `germinable-cosey-vireo`, closed) — only its comment `:28` names `bridge_state/`. Tracker-side `<tracker>/.bridge_state/` (bindings, projects, prev_snapshot, last-pass) is committed state and is **not** renamed.\n- **`MutationAction` pairs**: `_VALID_COMBINATIONS` (`mutation.py:37-42`) admits `(inbound, delete)` and `(inbound, probe)`; `typed_dispatch._build_leaves` (`:55-66`) registers no handler for either — dead.\n- **`outbound_fields.py`** (675 LOC): the only production importer is `adapters/jira/backend.py:26,70` (`_map_local_to_jira_fields`). `_extract_jira_field`, `_assignee_matches`, `_local_matches_prev`, `_jira_matches_prev`, `_parent_clear_is_managed`, `_resolve_reporter_account_id`, `_diff_reporter`, `_diff_fields`, `_INBOUND_MIRRORED_FIELDS` (`:246-675`) have zero production callers (re-homed in `outbound_field_diff.py`); tests still exercise `_diff_fields` (`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_baseline_arbitration.py`, `test_diff_assignee_permissive.py`, `test_diff_assignee_unmappable_converges.py`, `tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:641,670,808`).\n- **Bridge hop chain**: `_bridge_runner._run(MODE_COMMANDS[profile])` (`:112-123,216`) → `rebar bridge sync` → `_cli/_bridge_commands.launch_reconciler` (`:51`, `subprocess.call`, no timeout, `engine_env`) → `python -m rebar_reconciler sync`.\n\n## Cross-epic line ownership\n\n- **Config epic** (`_config_sources.py`, `config.py`, `_deprecations.py`): E3 does **not** edit them (`reconciler_repo_root` `config.py:622-652` is consumed unchanged); the only config-adjacent E3 edit is the comment `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:665` (S6).\n- **CLI epic** (`_cli/_registry.py`): untouched by E3. E3 owns `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:144-151` (S1) and `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py:31-51,147-161,188-189` (S1); the CLI epic owns everything else in those files.\n- **Operator sanction required** (S1, S2): value-preserving key re-spells in `.github/complexity-baseline.json` (6 keys) and `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (29 keys) — stated in each commit message; no ceiling or count changes.","timestamp":1788807743292713351},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Child stories created (all `story`, priority 2, tags `complexity-reduction` + `breaking-pass-4`, parent this epic; cites on origin/main 083620b0):\n\n- **S1** `gunshy-symmetric-barnacle` (`bf96-5776-6a97-420f`) — Move the reconciler to `rebar.reconciler` and delete every by-path loader (package move, `_loader.py` + all `lazy_load`/`spec_from_file_location`/`sys.path.insert` sites gone, `engine_env` drops PYTHONPATH, 6 complexity-baseline keys re-spelled). depends_on: none.\n- **S2** `emblematic-apostolic-mouse` (`4b2a-e417-30ed-4f3a`) — Delete the test-side engine-root machinery and rename `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` to `tests/unit/reconciler` (`_engine_path.py`, `_one_engine_root`, shadow bridge, root-convention tests deleted; 29 mechanism-baseline keys re-spelled + `--update-stale`). depends_on: `gunshy-symmetric-barnacle`.\n- **S3** `unadhesive-caloric-sapsucker` (`f75f-5d85-7b9a-4d86`) — Add `run_guarded_pass` as the one guarded core for the CLI, library and MCP `bridge_sync` (bug fix: library/MCP live pass now takes the lock, heartbeats, honors pause, publishes last-pass from the disposition). depends_on: `gunshy-symmetric-barnacle`.\n- **S4** `chippable-potty-dipper` (`cfbd-97a9-ff1d-4945`) — Spawn `python -m rebar.reconciler` directly from `_bridge_runner` and reap the process group on timeout (`MODE_ARGS`, `_spawn_bounded`, `start_new_session`, engine child owns exit codes). depends_on: `unadhesive-caloric-sapsucker`.\n- **S5** `captious-tangled-pigeon` (`fc96-b268-b737-4b8b`) — Delete the three retired `REBAR_RECONCILER_*` rollback toggles and make fail-loud unconditional (`CREATE_ROUTE`, `WRITE_FACADE`, `FAIL_SILENT_NOOP`; `--update-stale` for the three `env_var` rows). depends_on: `emblematic-apostolic-mouse`.\n- **S6** `senile-especial-herring` (`115f-4b98-3df5-48f7`) — Delete the dormant summary-executor, payload-shadow and `_concurrency` modules and the dead half of `outbound_fields` (typed-only `applier.apply`, explicit 10-pair `_VALID_COMBINATIONS`). depends_on: `captious-tangled-pigeon`.\n- **S7** `paper-ionic-ugandakob` (`ad8a-38e7-44d3-4662`) — Retire `_call_with_retry` so handlers make a single transport attempt (ADR 0103 S3; `ticket_plans` required, legacy `remaining` loop deleted). depends_on: `senile-especial-herring`.\n- **S8** `cob-portable-springbok` (`e6ee-ae52-8e5d-4917`) — Move reconciler scratch from `bridge_state/` to `.rebar/bridge/` with keep-last-N retention (`scratch_retention.py`, prune on persisted pass: 5 snapshots / 5 sync logs / 30 alert days). depends_on: `emblematic-apostolic-mouse`.\n\nEvery story carries a recorded file impact. S1 has an implementation-detail first comment (line cites, the six baseline keys, the `sys.modules` inventory, release note) plus the operator-sanction comment; S2 carries the mechanism-ratchet comment (deleted autouse fixtures + `tests/_engine_path.py` helper) plus the operator-sanction comment; S5 carries the mechanism-ratchet comment (the three env vars).","timestamp":1788807774684230994},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review 2026-10-18 returned BLOCK on one move: S4 specified \"reaps the process group\" without naming the existing shared helper, so a reviewer could not tell whether a second reaper would be written. Description updated: S4 and AC3 now name `rebar._proc.reap_process_group` (`src/rebar/_proc.py:38`, already the reaper for `grounding/harness.py`, `acli_subprocess.py`, and `wiki_render.py`) as the only reaper, and AC3 states the in-session checks: a monkeypatch test on the `_bridge_runner` import site, a real child-plus-grandchild timeout test asserting both pids are gone, and a grep proving no `os.kill`/`killpg`/`SIG*` call site was added outside `_proc.py`. The epic's 15 advisory findings (criterion-6 ownership propagation to children, lease-failure disposition example) are left for the story authors; none blocks.","timestamp":1792363374040837964}],"created_at":1788806584923371276,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2a981578-7abb-4437-861a-c7cbf5abe026","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1768-5b6f-958a-43e9"},{"link_uuid":"d2e38eef-8429-4a39-9c63-7a6cef80b854","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"10ae-1ef7-97c9-4645"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe Jira reconciler lives at `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` as a separate top-level package that 47 source files load by path (`lazy_load`, `spec_from_file_location`, `sys.path.insert(engine_dir)`), with a mirrored test-side loader complex (`tests/_engine_path.py`, three `conftest.py` bridges, shadow-package fixtures). The bridge runs through a three-hop chain (`_bridge_runner` -> `rebar bridge sync` -> `python -m rebar_reconciler`), the library's `_lib_ops._bridge_run` bypasses the guarded core so an MCP `bridge_sync` runs an unlocked live pass (a bug), three retired rollback toggles (`REBAR_RECONCILER_CREATE_ROUTE`, `_WRITE_FACADE`, `_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP`) still gate code paths, five dormant modules and one dead half-module remain, `_call_with_retry` survives past ADR 0103 S3, and `bridge_state/` accumulates at the repo root with no retention. The operator approved the package move, the guarded-core bug fix, the middle-hop collapse (subprocess boundary kept), the toggle and dead-code deletions after independent confirmation, and keep-last-N retention (2026-09-06). Every finding is resolved on origin/main 083620b0 in this epic's first comment. This epic writes no ADR: the consolidated reconciler record ADR 0119 is written by the docs/ADR epic's consolidation story after this epic's package move lands, so that it cites the final `rebar.reconciler` paths.\n\nOperator sanction recorded here: the two move stories carry value-preserving key re-spells in `.github/complexity-baseline.json` (6 keys, S1) and `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (29 keys, S2) with no ceiling or count change; the test-side story (S2, which deletes autouse fixtures and a `tests/_*.py` helper) and the toggle-deletion story (S5, which deletes three `env_var` rows) each run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in the same change, after the key re-spell, because `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` requires the baseline to match the live tree (precedent commit 81da792). Each such change states this sanction in its commit message.\n\nProcess-group reaping reuses the existing shared helper, it is not reimplemented: `rebar._proc.reap_process_group` (`src/rebar/_proc.py`, the leaf stdlib-only module introduced for bug d843) already implements the `start_new_session` group-leader reap that S4 needs (SIGTERM, grace, SIGKILL, bounded drain, ESRCH/EPERM-guarded, parameterised by grace/drain/label/logger) and is already the reaper for the grounding harness and `acli_subprocess`. S4 calls it and adds no second reaper; a new `kill`/`killpg` call site under `src/rebar/` outside `_proc.py` is a defect in S4.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar.reconciler` is an ordinary subpackage: no `lazy_load`, `spec_from_file_location`, or `sys.path.insert` engine loader remains under `src/` or `tests/`, and `python -m rebar.reconciler --help` works from a bare install. Checked by the repo-wide grep in the move stories and `make verify`.\n- [ ] The CLI, the library, and the MCP `bridge_sync` tool all run a live pass through one guarded core (`run_guarded_pass`) that takes the reconciler lease. Checked by the guarded-pass story's lock test over all three entry points.\n- [ ] `_bridge_runner` spawns `python -m rebar.reconciler` directly with `start_new_session=True` and, on timeout, reaps the process group through `rebar._proc.reap_process_group`; the `rebar bridge sync` hop is gone. Checked in-session by the runner story's subprocess tests: one test monkeypatches `reap_process_group` at the `_bridge_runner` import site and asserts it is called once with the child's pid on a forced timeout; one test spawns a real child that forks a grandchild, forces the timeout, and asserts neither pid survives (`os.kill(pid, 0)` raises `ProcessLookupError`); and `git grep -nE 'os\\.kill(pg)?\\(|signal\\.SIG(TERM|KILL)' -- src/rebar/reconciler src/rebar/_bridge_runner*` prints nothing, which proves no second reaper was written.\n- [ ] The three retired toggles, the five dormant modules, the dead half of `outbound_fields.py`, the two dead `MutationAction` pairs, and `_call_with_retry` are deleted with their tests; `make lint` reports `new=0` on both ratchets. Checked by grep and the ratchet output in each story.\n- [ ] Bridge scratch lives under `.rebar/bridge/` with keep-last-5 snapshots and sync logs and a 30-day alert window, pruned on every persisted pass. Checked by the retention story's tests.\n- [ ] Release notes and CHANGELOG record the package rename, the deleted env vars, and the `bridge_state/` move. Checked by the docs gates in `make verify`.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- S1 package move (`rebar.reconciler`, delete by-path loaders): criterion 1 for `src/`, part of criterion 6.\n- S2 test-side loader deletion and `tests/unit/reconciler` rename: criterion 1 for `tests/`; depends on S1.\n- S3 `run_guarded_pass` guarded core (bug fix): criterion 2; depends on S1.\n- S4 `_bridge_runner` direct spawn + process-group reap via `rebar._proc.reap_process_group`: criterion 3; depends on S3.\n- S5 delete the three retired toggles (fail-loud unconditional): criterion 4 part; depends on S2.\n- S6 delete dormant modules, dead halves, dead `MutationAction` pairs: criterion 4 part; depends on S5.\n- S7 retire `_call_with_retry`: criterion 4 part; depends on S6.\n- S8 `.rebar/bridge/` with keep-last-N retention: criterion 5; depends on S2.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","1768-5b6f-958a-43e9"],["relates_to","10ae-1ef7-97c9-4645"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Move the Jira reconciler into `rebar.reconciler`, collapse the bridge hop chain, and delete its retired toggles and dead code","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5d43c933-8059-473a-9357-d32cde4230de","2a981578-7abb-4437-861a-c7cbf5abe026","d2e38eef-8429-4a39-9c63-7a6cef80b854","4a76ed94-6538-497b-b15a-5e4f4bf5ad3e","c64255c7-3859-41a8-8d1e-f2d4528c7554","e79f44a0-547b-4421-823c-5d6d3f79644f","39734fe7-287b-4b1f-b2af-83ad2c7c1ce0","e640784b-6be9-4390-8d0f-026c5c584eec","ea3b76b7-c6d2-44e7-b5cd-74202f01f9b8","b45d91f0-6b7d-4530-8398-25fc049a041f","42d293ae-5f13-4c4d-ad81-ae4ef4a3de27"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792423248357563002,"uuid":"bdf911f5-efab-4774-a572-7fb00aae06be"}